        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ਮਾਂਜਣਾ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਮਾਂਜਣਾ — mānjṇā — \"to scrub (pots)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਮੈਂ ਰਾਤ ਨੂੰ ਭਾਂਡੇ ਮਾਂਜਦੀ ਹਾਂ। maiṁ rāt nū̃ bhāṇḍe mānjdī hāṁ. At night I scrub the pots."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ਮੈਂ ਭਾਂਡੇ ਮਾਂਜੇ, maiṁ bhāṇḍe mānje."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਮਾਂਜਣਾ (mānjṇā) is inherited from Sanskrit mārjati, \"wipes off, rubs clean\"; CDIAL lists Punjabi mā̃jṇā, \"to rub\" (CDIAL 10080). The pot-scouring sense is CDIAL's Lahnda gloss: mā̃jhaṇ, \"to clean out a vessel with sand or ashes\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
